S-117: board A's charger U3 (BQ25731), inductor and frequency. MESHSAT-1357, stream s117. Desk arithmetic on the
makers' figures; nothing is built or measured. INFERRED: curve readings (inductance under current; the FET's gate
charge at 6 V, plateau and RDS(on) at 6 V). Currents at eta = 1 (an upper bound).

1. THE CHARGER'S CURRENTS (buck mode; IL = VIN x IIN / VSYS)
pt     VIN    IIN   VSYS   IL (A)  what
G1   20.70   5.70  10.00    11.80  as generated: the front end's 5.7 A maximum into a pack at its 10.0 V CUV (the bound)
G2   20.70   5.70  10.60    11.13  as generated: the same input, the pack at its 2.65 V a cell cut-off
G3   20.70   5.70  14.40     8.19  as generated: the same input, the pack at its 14.4 V nominal
G4   20.00   5.00  14.40     6.94  as generated: the front end's 5.0 A typical limit, 20.0 V, nominal pack
G5   20.70   4.15  14.50     5.92  as generated with FW-A16 revised (a1elec E1): IIN_HOST 4.15 A
A1   20.70   6.20  14.50     8.85  Option A(i) drafted (a1elec E2): IIN_HOST 6.2 A at the model's 14.5 V node
A2   20.70   6.45  10.00    13.35  Option A(i) bound: U3's 6.35 A clamp plus 0.1 A, pack at 10.0 V
S1   20.70   5.70   9.00    13.11  sensitivity only: the secondary protector's 9.0 V UV (the primary has failed)

2. THE INDUCTOR AT EACH POINT: ripple (Equation 3), peak, RMS (Equation 8), against the maker's Isat and Irms
   nominal = L nominal x its DC-bias fall, fS typical; worst = L at -20 % x its fall, fS at the table minimum.
   Equation 2 (p.85): ISAT >= ICHG + IRIPPLE / 2, read at the worst ripple. Irms: the maker's 40 C rise figure.

