5. THE GATE DRIVE THE CHARGER'S OWN 6 V REGULATOR MUST SUPPLY (REGN feeds both low-side drivers and, through the
   bootstrap capacitors, both high-side drivers). In buck mode Q1 and Q2 (board A's Q7 and Q8) switch every cycle and
   Q4 is held on (Table 9-3, p.27), so IREGN = (Qg(Q7) + Qg(Q8)) x fS. SLUSE66A 8.5, p.11: VREGN_REG 5.7 / 6.0 / 6.3 V
   is specified for 0 to 60 mA; IREGN_LIM, the current limit with the converter enabled, is 50 min / 65 typ mA.
   Qg at 6 V: 75 nC INFERRED (Figure 4); the table's 58 nC at 4.5 V is a floor for a 6 V drive.
   fS             Qg 58 nC     Qg 75 nC   against 60 mA spec / 50 mA minimum limit
   min 400 kHz      39.4 mA      51.0 mA   straddles the 50 mA minimum limit
   400 kHz         46.4 mA      60.0 mA   straddles the 50 mA minimum limit
   max 400 kHz      53.4 mA      69.0 mA   OVER the 50 mA minimum limit
   min 800 kHz      78.9 mA     102.0 mA   OVER the 50 mA minimum limit
   800 kHz         92.8 mA     120.0 mA   OVER the 50 mA minimum limit
   max 800 kHz     106.7 mA     138.0 mA   OVER the 50 mA minimum limit
   In BUCK-BOOST mode all four FETs switch (Table 9-3) and the demand doubles; the maker states the three modes by
   the VBUS and VBAT combination and gives no threshold for the transition (9.3.10, p.27), so whether U3 enters it
   near a full pack (16.8 V against 20 V in) is not stated. Four CSD18510Q5B switching:
   400 kHz typical: 92.8 to 120.0 mA against the 50 mA minimum limit
   800 kHz typical: 185.6 to 240.0 mA against the 50 mA minimum limit
   The same current is drawn from VBUS20 through REGN's linear regulator: at 20.7 V and the typical fS the gate
   drive takes 1.24 W at 400 kHz, of which the regulator's own drop, 0.88 W, is dissipated inside U3; with the
   JEDEC RthJA of 37.2 C/W (8.4, p.9) that drop alone is a 33 K rise of U3's junction over its surroundings.
   drive takes 2.48 W at 800 kHz, of which the regulator's own drop, 1.76 W, is dissipated inside U3; with the
   JEDEC RthJA of 37.2 C/W (8.4, p.9) that drop alone is a 66 K rise of U3's junction over its surroundings.
   (JEDEC's board is not board A; the figure orders the two rows, it does not predict U3's temperature.)
